The desktop stops waking hundreds of times a second in the background.

USER 2026-10-04: "Battery usage on android is horrendous, we need to
make this thing yield a lot more and only activate when needed".
AndroWish builds SDL with SDL_ANDROID_BLOCK_ON_PAUSE=0, so a paused
desktop keeps running Tcl (its background handler closes the streams
and stops the polls, android.tcl) — and three polling loops with it.
Measured on the phone 2026-10-04, backgrounded, per thread: ~5% of a
core for as long as Android kept it the "previous app" (oom adj 700,
never frozen), and they run in the foreground too:

- SDL 2.0.6's SDL_WaitEventTimeout waits by polling, SDL_Delay(10).
  Paused, it polls at 4 Hz; the resume is the one event that matters
  then, and 250 ms is no wait to notice it.
- SDL_config_android.h lacks HAVE_SEM_TIMEDWAIT, so SDL_SemWaitTimeout
  polls with SDL_Delay(1): the timer thread, between sdl2tk's frame
  ticks, woke ~1000 times a second. Bionic has always had
  sem_timedwait.
- sdl2tk caps Tcl's every wait at 20 ms to look at its X queue (the
  Tcl thread and its notifier traded ~114 bytes a second through the
  notifier's pipe). In the background the cap is 250 ms; Tcl's own
  timers and sockets wake it as before.

--- a/jni/SDL2/include/SDL_config_android.h	2026-10-04 21:16:58.534339660 +0200
